block content
    h1 Anal Fistulas
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/anal-fistula/symptoms-causes/syc-20352871") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote An anal fistula — also called fistula-in-ano — is a tunnel that develops between the inside of the anus and the outside skin around the anus. The anus is the muscular opening at the end of the digestive tract where stool exits the body.
